(Stage 1d — a `value`-returning call brings its tag back in r11, so reading
 the result directly must dispatch on that tag rather than on the call's
 static type. Printing one used to render the raw payload (a string pointer
 or IEEE bits as an integer) and a predicate on one always answered
 "number", because neither consulted the returned tag.)

To "echo" with a value called "v". Return a value, v.

a list called "m" is [1, "two", 3.5].
For each item in m,
  print "echo" of item.

For each item in m,
  If "echo" of item is a text, print "T".
  Otherwise if "echo" of item is a decimal, print "D".
  Otherwise print "N".
